# SDLC ecosystem (PersonaLearn)

## Platform roles

| System | Owns |
|--------|------|
| **Jira (PSL)** | Tickets, sprint, status, blockers |
| **Confluence (PLEARN)** | Specs, ADRs, release notes, retros |
| **GitHub** | Code, branches, PRs, CI, release tags |
| **Slack (#personalearn-dev)** | Notifications only — not source of truth |

Notion is **out of the official traceability chain**. Do not create SDLC artifacts there.

**Confluence hub:** https://nervustechnologies.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/PLEARN/overview

## Golden thread

Every unit of work traces to `PSL-N`:

```
Jira ticket → Confluence spec → GitHub branch/PR → Slack notification
```

If it does not link to `PSL-N`, treat it as unofficial until triaged into Jira.

## Jira workflow (PSL)

| Status | Meaning | Agent action |
|--------|---------|--------------|
| **To Do** | Backlog; refine until spec linked | Do not branch |
| **In Progress** | Branch exists; active implementation | On "implement PSL-N" after branch created |
| **Review** | PR open; CI/review in flight | When PR is opened |
| **Blocker** | Blocked on dependency or external factor | When blockers cannot be resolved in-session |
| **Done** | Merged to `develop` | After squash merge (user approves merge) |

Complements `git-workflow.mdc` — follow both rules together.

## Labels (Jira + GitHub PRs)

Apply one **area** and one **type** label on every ticket and PR:

**Area:** `area-auth`, `area-dashboard`, `area-classes`, `area-ai-rag`, `area-infra`, `area-docs`

**Type:** `type-feature`, `type-bug`, `type-chore`, `type-tech-debt`

**Sprint:** use Jira **Sprint** field (primary). Optional label: `sprint-N`.

Reference vocabulary: Jira PSL-35 (do not delete).

## Ticket description template

When creating or refining Jira tickets, include:

```markdown
## Ready checklist
- [ ] Confluence spec linked
- [ ] Acceptance criteria defined
- [ ] No open blocker links
- [ ] Area + type labels set

## Acceptance criteria
- ...

## Spec
Duplicate https://nervustechnologies.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/PLEARN/pages/4325405 (Product requirements template)
```

