## Agent playbook

Before any implementation:

1. `getJiraIssue(PSL-N)` — read ACs, labels, sprint, linked spec
2. Check **blocks** links — abort if prerequisites are not Done
3. Confirm ticket is in sprint or explicitly prioritized by user

During implementation (with `git-workflow.mdc`):

4. Branch from `origin/develop` → `{feature|fix|chore|docs}/PSL-N-*`
5. Transition Jira → **In Progress**; comment with branch name
6. Implement and test; commit only when user asks
7. Open PR targeting `develop` with `PSL-N` in title; apply matching area/type labels; set milestone **Sprint 2** when in current sprint
8. Transition Jira → **Review**; comment with PR URL and Vercel preview
9. Babysit CI until green; do not merge without user approval
10. On merge → transition **Done**; post to `#personalearn-dev` (channel `C0BDURJTXR8`)

## Confluence structure

Under [PersonaLearn](https://nervustechnologies.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/PLEARN/overview) (`PLEARN` space) — use native templates above; populate per ticket/sprint, not upfront.

## GitHub

- **Milestone:** current sprint (e.g. Sprint 2) on PRs
- **Release tags:** `v0.x.0` on `main` when promoting `develop` → `main`
- **GitHub Projects:** not used — Jira board is the backlog

## Human gates

Agents must stop and ask for:

- Merge approval
- Commit (unless user explicitly requests)
- Scope changes beyond ticket ACs
- Creating new Jira tickets without triage (use `triage-issue` skill for bugs)
